{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed","id":1283895,"title":"Story idea: The attempt to bring back a Lost Breed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-31T05:33:45-08:00","id":1283895,"title":"Story idea: The attempt to bring back a Lost Breed","content":"Hey guys and gals,<br /> <br /> so I'm working on a chronical in the more or less far future and would like to discuss some... hypothetical possibilities.<br /> We have a fera group in W20.<br /> <br /> I think about a chronical about the try - and most likely failure - to create a new or restore a lost changing breed. My intention is not to shake up the whole WOD canon nor to create a uber breed players can play in the future.<br /> Just the... quest of an incarna to bring an advantage into the war. In a slightly longer run than the generic lets-raid-a-pentex-base garou manner.<br /> <br /> The most obvious question would be: what lost breed? Or better: what kind of breed does the world need now the most? Apis to enhance the chances for successful breeding? Grondr to deal with the envoirmental damage on earth? Or something entirely other like were-eagles as some kind of diplomats to reunite the existing breeds?<br /> <br /> BUT the most important question would be: which incarna would contemplate such plan? I would like to have some powerful spirit like falcon or bear. Someone whose authority is unquestionable. I really don't need players who question the honesty of the sprit to help gaia. So can you help me with a good candidate? In whos nature would be such dangerous yet promising plan?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for now<br /> lastlostboy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T10:51:15-08:00","id":1283967,"title":"","content":"From established lore, Bear is one of the most powerful healing spirits, so he is your best bet. His children are the only ones who currently have a way of raising the dead. Mind you that way wouldn't work for this scenario but it shows how strong in the healing arts they are.<br /> <br /> Deviating from that, you could always go with a new spirit though, something no one has ever seen. The character may never see the spirit directly for a long time. They could only communicate through lesser spirits of the new incarna's brood. They wouldn't know if their benefactor is truely benevolent or maleficent until it was too late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T15:11:49-08:00","id":1284016,"title":"","content":"Help the children of the Bat redeem Bat. Bat teaches one of them the Rite to make a new Camadoz. This is a SIMPLE plot but.. not an easy one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T15:23:33-08:00","id":1284225,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Were-whales, the Song of Gaia?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T01:00:16-08:00","id":1284300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1283967#post1283967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviating from that, you could always go with a new spirit though, something no one has ever seen. The character may never see the spirit directly for a long time. They could only communicate through lesser spirits of the new incarna's brood. They wouldn't know if their benefactor is truely benevolent or maleficent until it was too late.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that would be the plan somehow or other. I would never let the incarna itself take stage, except maybe in the finale or epilog. It would communicate only through avatars. I'm not a fan of roleplaying such powerful enitities directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284016#post1284016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Help the children of the Bat redeem Bat. Bat teaches one of them the Rite to make a new Camadoz. This is a SIMPLE plot but.. not an easy one?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I acutually thought about too. But I don't exactly know what happened. Can you help me?<br /> So Bat foresaw the death of their children and went crazy? When the Spanish came and with them the garou they only saw weird blood sacrificing changers and thought of the wyrm and killed them all? <br /> What were their job? What would be their job in the present? Didn't corax assimilate their job somehow?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284225#post1284225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Were-whales, the Song of Gaia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even tho they're not changers, with Rorqual there are close enough gaian worshippers to not bring another mammal changer in the soup.<br /> But I had merfolk already in my past stories so a marine born changer might be an interesting idea. Maybe something Quyrl related so there would be some disagreement about whether or not it's a good idea to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T05:13:46-08:00","id":1284323,"title":"","content":"Have you already read &quot;Shattered Dreams&quot;? It's a campaign about a temporal mess where past and present blend together and the role for the PC is to put things back the way they were. This also means that you'll have the chance to meet and interact with not-yet-extinct groups of Fera.<br /> <br /> I spent some thoughts about running it with players as a Fera party and make them realize, in the end, that the only way to save Gaia is by accepting the extinction of their whole breed (and their subsequent return to nonexistence), but you could easily use the same plot hooks and have your characters change history in a way that brings back a lost breed without breaking the world.<br /> (Shattered Dreams is also a nice source for Garou history).<br /> <br /> If you'd rather keep it more conventional then I'd say, in addition to the others, you could consider the Grondr. Perhaps the Skull Pigs can be cleansed from the Wyrm-taint and brought back to Gaia (it might require more than one generation, though), and once the Grondr kin are pure again they might have some chance to give birth to a new Grondr; maybe the last part of the campaign could revolve around fertility issues, selective breeding and spirit-enhancing techniques to help them breed true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T06:42:51-08:00","id":1284331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284300#post1284300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's something I acutually thought about too. But I don't exactly know what happened. Can you help me?<br /> So Bat foresaw the death of their children and went crazy? When the Spanish came and with them the garou they only saw weird blood sacrificing changers and thought of the wyrm and killed them all?<br /> What were their job? What would be their job in the present? Didn't corax assimilate their job somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It turns into a bat and drinks blood&quot; &quot;IT MUST BE A VAMPIRE KILL IT&quot; &quot;Don't we have scent of the true form&quot; &quot;SHUT UP THAT'S WYRM TALK&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;oh shit we killed another Fera breed..how could we Shadowlords have known..&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly doubling the information that's spread between the various fera so they are better informed can only be a good thing. They also might have been instramental in a &quot;Purelands&quot; mutibreed setup. You get them back. They help Balam rediscover some of their secrets same with the Uktena etc...<br /> <br /> Also its relatively &quot;Simple&quot; and can justify not needing to have a previous one or having to wait 2-10 years if new one is pregant. since like Corax they use a rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T08:00:46-08:00","id":1284348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284300#post1284300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even tho they're not changers, with Rorqual there are close enough gaian worshippers to not bring another mammal changer in the soup.<br /> But I had merfolk already in my past stories so a marine born changer might be an interesting idea. Maybe something Quyrl related so there would be some disagreement about whether or not it's a good idea to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I just want to relive the glory days of RIFTS Undersea, where one could play a humpback whale who had the fly fishing skill.<br /> <br /> More seriously, were-bison as a North American counterpart to the Apis might be interesting.<br /> <br /> Also, there's the were-orangutans mentioned in 1st ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T08:02:38-08:00","id":1284349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284331#post1284331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It turns into a bat and drinks blood&quot; &quot;IT MUST BE A VAMPIRE KILL IT&quot; &quot;Don't we have scent of the true form&quot; &quot;SHUT UP THAT'S WYRM TALK&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You made me laugh hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T13:23:09-08:00","id":1284384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284331#post1284331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It turns into a bat and drinks blood&quot; &quot;IT MUST BE A VAMPIRE KILL IT&quot; &quot;Don't we have scent of the true form&quot; &quot;SHUT UP THAT'S WYRM TALK&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read the Mokol\u00e9 breed book a few weeks ago and that's exactly what happend in the book's comprehensive story...<br /> <br /> &quot;THEY HAVE LIZARD FORMS, THEY MUST BE WYRM!&quot;<br /> &quot;They don't smell like wyrm.&quot;<br /> &quot;LOOK AT THEM!&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh sHIT, THEY LOOK LIKE WYRM!&quot;<br /> <br /> God, I hate garou so much... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284323#post1284323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you already read &quot;Shattered Dreams&quot;? It's a campaign about a temporal mess where past and present blend together and the role for the PC is to put things back the way they were. This also means that you'll have the chance to meet and interact with not-yet-extinct groups of Fera.<br /> <br /> I spent some thoughts about running it with players as a Fera party and make them realize, in the end, that the only way to save Gaia is by accepting the extinction of their whole breed (and their subsequent return to nonexistence), but you could easily use the same plot hooks and have your characters change history in a way that brings back a lost breed without breaking the world.<br /> (Shattered Dreams is also a nice source for Garou history).<br /> <br /> If you'd rather keep it more conventional then I'd say, in addition to the others, you could consider the Grondr. Perhaps the Skull Pigs can be cleansed from the Wyrm-taint and brought back to Gaia (it might require more than one generation, though), and once the Grondr kin are pure again they might have some chance to give birth to a new Grondr; maybe the last part of the campaign could revolve around fertility issues, selective breeding and spirit-enhancing techniques to help them breed true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no. Sorry. Time travel or time warp is a red flag for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The skull-pig idea is pretty good because it's comes with more or less a big goal already: redeem the skull-pigs.<br /> But Lians argument with the long term stuff is good too. &quot;Hurr-durr magic!&quot; might be a better straight forward solution to not have to wait for generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T00:02:49-08:00","id":1284454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284384#post1284384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Lians argument with the long term stuff is good too. &quot;Hurr-durr magic!&quot; might be a better straight forward solution to not have to wait for generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Grondr recovery is something more for a generational campaign... you open the way to cleanse the skull pigs, your sons manage to purify them, your nephew help them get in shape and your grand-grandchildren 150 years from now sees the first Grondr come back to Earth with his ancestors sharing the moment through his very eyes.<br /> <br /> Or I guess you could meddle a bit with the required time. Introducing a mage, if you like crossovers, or petitioning a time spirit (like Chronos), or bringing them to some realm where time flows faster (like the Legendaries)... but let's be honest, for a story set in a short time span the Camatzotz are probably a better target.<br /> <br /> But you could always say that you found the last Apis in the Deep Umbra, trapped in Malfeas or lost in the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T00:30:25-08:00","id":1284459,"title":"","content":"Beast breed generations aren't super long.. that's why we can domesticate animals iRL. It might require a jump of 20 years to see much progress but its not intrinsically generational. OR you could be a kitsune bene Geseret<br /> <br /> But speaking of Bene Gesseret lets get back to the apis. So having done a shallow dive into the world that is the bovine genome.. the whole &quot;They can't exist because no Aurochs&quot; in a world where there are various wild dog Garou.. seems kind of off. There's a lot of easy interbreeding between the various members of the Bos genius and a number of them maintain undomesticated variants. Similarly the related Bison genus is interfertile with Bos.. and the European bison genome has 10 percent admixture from Aurochs..<br /> <br /> Right with that in mind.. what were the Apis? Well part of it was they were the bene Geneseret of Gaia. the Master manipulators of bloodlines and breeding, and the Bos setup is so intermixed perhaps they never left rather than going into hiding... or perhaps they planned some elaborate scheme... to be reborn when the time is right...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T02:09:50-08:00","id":1284470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284459#post1284459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast breed generations aren't super long.. that's why we can domesticate animals iRL. It might require a jump of 20 years to see much progress but its not intrinsically generational.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not.. but the skull pigs were corrupted for so long that now they have a skull for head and bear little resemblance to actual boars. I doubt that you could just cast a rite of cleansing and be done, it's going to take time to cleanse them (i mean, you can't even use the Erebus) and even after that they're going to need the time to revert back to their original shape. And since the chance of spawning wereboars between kinfolks is exceedengly low you'll need a lot of them and quite a bit of time.<br /> This is why I was talking about generational campaign. Of course this is just my take, but I wouldn't have them just healed overnight with a wave of Gaia's hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T14:39:45-08:00","id":1284578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1284470#post1284470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe not.. but the skull pigs were corrupted for so long that now they have a skull for head and bear little resemblance to actual boars. I doubt that you could just cast a rite of cleansing and be done, it's going to take time to cleanse them (i mean, you can't even use the Erebus) and even after that they're going to need the time to revert back to their original shape. And since the chance of spawning wereboars between kinfolks is exceedengly low you'll need a lot of them and quite a bit of time.<br /> This is why I was talking about generational campaign. Of course this is just my take, but I wouldn't have them just healed overnight with a wave of Gaia's hand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there's a middle ground between multiple human generations and done over night. 20 years might show some results","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T14:48:34-08:00","id":1285061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed#post1283895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most obvious question would be: what lost breed? Or better: what kind of breed does the world need now the most? Apis to enhance the chances for successful breeding? Grondr to deal with the envoirmental damage on earth? Or something entirely other like were-eagles as some kind of diplomats to reunite the existing breeds?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about one where the process has already started? Having the Apis or Grondr back would have been good for the last few thousand years, but it's too late for them to help now. The Last Battle is coming, and without shock troopers to lead the charge, the Changing Breeds have already lost. Gaia needs the *real* Kerasi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13544-impeesa","name":"Impeesa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T23:50:33-08:00","id":1285139,"title":"","content":"Damnit I hate misclicking on my phone!!!<br /> <br /> <br /> So I say Apis all the way! And Phoenix as the Patron calling upon her aspect of Resurrection. Maybe even in the Form of the Benu Bird of Ra. It\u2019s fitting with the Apis and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T06:14:10-08:00","id":1285224,"title":"","content":"There are several options:<br /> <br /> The canon background points to these possibilities:<br /> <br /> Camazotz: There a faction of the Shadowlords restoring the sanity of the Totem Bat. These werewolves have recibed some gifts of it.<br /> <br /> Apis and Grond: In the Guide to the Changing Breeds W20 there are advices about bring back this Breeds. I think it would be neccesary get the favor of Totems as Bull or Boar.<br /> <br /> Samsa: These werecockroachs are an artificial creation of Pentex, but the Totem Cockroach seem interested in them. Perhaps with the hepl of the characters the Samsa can transform in a Breed loyal to Gaia.<br /> <br /> A new Breed: The Mokol\u00e9 know ancient gifts and rites that allow create new Breeds (as the Kucha Ekundu or the Bunyip). Perhaps the characters should be negotiate with the weresaurians and a spirit that protects the new Breed as her Totem. Some time ago I followed this option to the creation of the Guar\u00e1, a Breed of were maned wolves (Chrysocyon brachiurus), with a role similar to the Nuwisha in South America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2250,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","user":"Magus","date":". 02-06-2019, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T10:22:41-08:00","id":1285281,"title":"","content":"So the following ran through my head:<br /> <br /> There's one entity that is almost indispensable for any of these scenarios. Gaia.<br /> <br /> So after an epic quest to get Gaia's blessing the characters finally meet one of her avatars and she is absolutely scathing. Oh, now the wolves are sorry for what they did. Now they want help. No dice, if she has to work with such disappointing protectors as the Garou, they have to live with the disappointment of their own actions. Her words are more than words, they are her incarnate anger and every time she opens her mouth it forces Rage rolls. Then she casts them out into the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> They are caught by Luna, who explains (and I'm translating this from her native cryptic words) that Gaia is more angry at herself. When she made the Garou (all of the Fera really, she knew immediately they were flawed. She could have made better protectors, ones who wouldn't destroy their siblings, but she would have had to destroy the Garou to do it. She couldn't do that to them. Her nature is not perfection it is working and growing and sickening and dying. She took the wolves in because of their flaws not despite them.<br /> <br /> The secret to getting Gaia's aid then is to bring back the Fera in question first, regardless of how flawed it is. Only then can Gaia embrace them and grant her blessing.<br /> <br /> Then Luna's eyes turn dark and she warns the characters that if they are going to go down this path they better do the very best they can. She's tired of seeing Gaia hurt, and if the pack breaks her heart again well she'll have to make the Galliard immortal just so they have time to sing about what she does to the rest of the pack.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:16:28-08:00","id":1285349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1285224#post1285224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A new Breed: The Mokol\u00e9 know ancient gifts and rites that allow create new Breeds (as the Kucha Ekundu or the Bunyip). Perhaps the characters should be negotiate with the weresaurians and a spirit that protects the new Breed as her Totem. Some time ago I followed this option to the creation of the Guar\u00e1, a Breed of were maned wolves (Chrysocyon brachiurus), with a role similar to the Nuwisha in South America.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a new Breed.. THat would just be more Nuwisha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T18:05:42-08:00","id":1285750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1283967#post1283967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From established lore, Bear is one of the most powerful healing spirits, so he is your best bet. His children are the only ones who currently have a way of raising the dead. Mind you that way wouldn't work for this scenario but it shows how strong in the healing arts they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia's Breath and Rite of Fighting the Death Bear are pretty serious powers but they only let you raise one person at a time. Fighting the Death Bear is only used to get Gurahl back because of the risk.<br /> BUT, you could petition Mangi to assist, it seems to protect the gateway between life and death. You might want to combine powers of Mangi, Pheonix, Anubis (If the Striders get on board with it) Which ever Native American Death Gods that your tribes can access (Camazotz was a Mayan death God, although most Mayan Gods seemed to be Death Gods)<br /> <br /> As well as looking at fallen Fera, the idea with Samsa <i>could</i> maybe work for all the Mockery Breeds. Quite a few people have mentioned that Pentex and the Wyrm couldn't have <span style=\"color:#008000\">Created</span> new breeds, only <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">corrupted</span> old ones using existing genes. That's more under the <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Wyrm</span> Perview","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T21:07:26-08:00","id":1285790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283895-story-idea-the-attempt-to-bring-back-a-lost-breed?p=1285750#post1285750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite a few people have mentioned that Pentex and the Wyrm couldn't have <span style=\"color:#008000\">Created</span> new breeds, only <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">corrupted</span> old ones using existing genes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that there are still the Flux realms or the Wyld Founts for whenever the Wyrm needs a bit of a creation power. The BSDs are not the Pentex but I can definively see them working together on this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}